body:
First acquisition-component court is ready for adversarial review under bead bd-01M188P265MZVEKBD5BBN34E6T: docs/design/movie-component-admission-ledger.md.

Proposed bounded disposition:
- FFmpeg 9.0.1 source coordinate and conservative LGPL-only probe recipe are paperwork-admitted; no decoder, executable, container, fixture codec surface, patent clearance, or native closure is admitted. Execution remains HELD.
- PySceneDetect 0.7.1 code and ContentDetector-only policy are paperwork-admitted; direct process_frame over atlas-indexed BGR24 frames is mandatory. PySceneDetect cannot decode or own time. Python/OpenCV/NumPy/native/container closure is unresolved, so execution remains HELD.
- All other named acquisition families are CandidateOnly, Deferred, or OwnerActionRequired with HoldUnknown; none inherit a code, weights, service, corpus, or runtime grant.
- F0 and F1 fixture manifests still determine the exact decoder and runtime surface. This document closes only the component-ledger leg and does not close overall B0, P1, source admission, owner actions, or authorize C1.

Please review especially:
1. whether the five status axes and non-inheritance laws are complete and non-overlapping;
2. whether any source/licence/runtime claim overreaches primary evidence;
3. whether FFmpeg and PySceneDetect are prevented from acquiring narrative/time/identity authority;
4. whether the held-vs-paperwork-admitted boundary is unmistakable;
5. whether any missing leaf should block documentation closure.

No packages, media, weights, containers, accounts, gated terms, credentials, or executions were used. The accepted architecture remains unlanded only because candidate cand-40W7YAE5N2EPS8M542GKEEZMS4 awaits chief authorization; P1 and B0 remain open.
